// =============================================================================
// 21. ENTITY OPTIONS
// =============================================================================

// A service layer everywhere — gives every entity a place to put business
// rules instead of pushing them into the Angular app.
service * with serviceClass

// Criteria-based querying (?fieldId.equals=, ?fieldId.in=, ...) everywhere.
// The old JDL enabled it on only 39 of 145 entities, which is why the frontend
// had to fetch-and-filter in the browser for the rest.
filter *

// Pagination for transactional / high-volume entities only.
// Everything in the `except` list is reference data that the UI loads whole
// into dropdowns — paginating those would silently truncate them to 20 rows.
//
// NOTE: both JHipster 8.7 and 9.4 print "the paginate option is deprecated,
// please use pagination instead" here, but neither actually accepts the
// `pagination` keyword — the lexer rejects it in both. `paginate` is the only
// parseable spelling as of 9.4.0. Ignore the warning.
paginate * with pagination except
  StatusCategory, Status, StatusValidChange,
  PartyType, RoleType, PartyClassificationType, PartyClassificationGroup,
  PartyIdentificationType, PartyRelationshipType,
  ContactMechPurpose, ContactMechType,
  GeoType, GeoAssocType, GeoPoint,
  ContentType,
  Department, ProductStore, SystemParameters, CustomTimePeriod,
  UomType, Uom, UomConversion,
  Catalogue, CatalogueCategoryType, CatalogueCategory,
  ProductCategoryType, ProductCategory,
  ProductType, ProductAssocType,
  ProductFeatureCategory, ProductFeatureType, ProductFeatureGroup,
  ProductFeatureApplType,
  ProductPriceType, ProductPricePurpose, KeywordType,
  FacilityType, FacilityGroupType, FacilityGroup, LocationType,
  InventoryItemType, Lot,
  ShoppingListType,
  OrderType, OrderItemType, SalesChannel, OrderAdjustmentType,
  InvoiceType, InvoiceItemType, InvoiceItemTypeMap,
  PaymentType, PaymentMethodType, PaymentGatewayConfig,
  TaxAuthority, TaxAuthorityRateType, TaxSlab,
  ShipmentType, ShipmentMethodType, CarrierShipmentMethod,
  FacilityCarrierShipment,
  CustRequestType, CustRequestCategory,
  QuoteType, ReturnHeaderType,
  TransactionCategory, TransactionType

// =============================================================================
// NOTES / DELIBERATE DECISIONS
// =============================================================================
//
// * No `dto * with mapstruct`. The current app serves JPA entities directly and
//   the whole Angular layer is written against that JSON shape. Adding DTOs
//   would change every payload. Add it later, per entity, if you want to
//   decouple the API from the schema.
//
// * Relationships stay unidirectional ManyToOne (child -> parent), as today.
//   Adding OneToMany inverse sides would make `GET /api/orders` serialise every
//   order line (N+1 + huge payloads). Fetch children with the criteria filters
//   instead: `GET /api/order-items?orderId.equals=42`.
//
// * `Order` is a SQL reserved word; JHipster maps it to table `jhi_order`
//   automatically. Same for `SystemParameters.key`/`value`.
//
// * No entity auditing (createdBy/createdDate/lastModifiedBy) — JHipster 8 core
//   has no JDL option for it. If you want it on every table, extend
//   `AbstractAuditingEntity` in the generated domain classes (or add a
//   `.jhipster` blueprint) as a post-generation step.
//
// * Renamed since p2p.jdl (none of these are referenced by the existing
//   Angular code, so the port is unaffected):
//     Invoice/Shipment: partyIdFrom/partyIdTo   -> fromParty/toParty
//     Payment:          partyIdFrom/partyIdTo   -> fromParty/toParty
//     ProductAssoc:     productIdTo             -> productTo
//     Order:            ctp                     -> customTimePeriod
//     Quote/CustRequest:ProductStore            -> productStore
//     FacilityGroup:    facilityGroup (self)    -> parentFacilityGroup
//     UomConversion:    convertionFactor        -> conversionFactor
//     InventoryItem:    activationValidTrue     -> activationValidThru
//     QuoteItem:        leadTime (Duration)     -> leadTimeDays (Integer)
//     CustRequest:      custEstimatedDuration   -> custEstimatedDurationDays
//     CashBookAttachment: product               -> cashBook
//
// * Dropped from p2p.jdl: Invoice.orderRefNo, orderDate, priority, isRushOrder,
//   needsInventoryIssuance, remainingSubTotal, deliveryDate, attr1..attr3
//   (unused Order copy-paste); OrderItem.fromInventoryItemId (duplicate of
//   fromInventoryItem); UomConversion.uom/uomTo (duplicate of fromUom/toUom);
//   CashBook.type/category/department/paymentMode (now FKs).
//
// * The Angular app calls `/api/users/create`, `/api/users/all`,
//   `/api/users/profiles`, `/api/tickets`, `/api/ticket-types`,
//   `/api/experiments` — none of these exist in the backend and none are
//   modelled here. They are dead references carried over from another codebase;
//   drop them when porting.
// =============================================================================
